//! Charter `H-DAG` models, generated by `proptest_scheduler_dag_models`.
//!
//! The successful-DAG oracle is the independent finite linear-extension
//! definition: every permutation of the graph's node indices is filtered by
//! the declared edge precedence relation and the lexicographically smallest
//! module-id sequence wins. It never calls
//! `slicer_scheduler::topological_sort` (`crates/slicer-scheduler/src/topology.rs`)
//! or copies a ready-queue/Kahn loop.
//!
//! The cyclic oracle is the nonempty-path remainder from
//! `slicer_sdk::test_support::property_testing::oracles::graph_cycle_remainder`
//! (`crates/slicer-sdk/src/test_support/property_testing/oracles/mod.rs`). It is
//! compared as a set against the validator's private sorter
//! (`crates/slicer-scheduler/src/validation.rs::validate_cycles`) and as a
//! lexically sorted `Vec` against the public sorter, because only the public
//! error `Vec` promises lexical order.
//!
//! Every successful DAG case also assembles a real plan at
//! `slicer_scheduler::build_execution_plan` from the real
//! `slicer_scheduler::topological_sort` output, `slicer_scheduler::SortedStageModules`
//! and `slicer_scheduler::bind_module_config_view` bindings, then checks the
//! compiled sequence, claims, access masks, `requires_modules`, paint-only
//! versus declaring-but-transparent dispatch semantics, the host
//! `Layer::PaintRegionAnnotation` insertion and the plan-built
//! `aggregated_region_split` against the table-derived declarations.
//!
//! `run_property` audits the composed strategy before `PropertyRun::check`:
//! the case mode is drawn from a non-shrinkable weighted selector, and a
//! fixed-seed `simplify()` walk asserts the mode tag, the shrunk body's oracle
//! invariants and the duplicate-destination flag never change.

